# D11. Runtime errors carry the JDK's own message text, for the errors a first course shows. Written
# from the pinned JDK's observed output only (clean room, D14): every message below was read off small
# programs run on Temurin 25.0.4.1; no OpenJDK source was opened.
#   - array index (compiler): the bounds check the strict-mode compiler inserts now throws
#     "Index 3 out of bounds for length 3"; a check for a possibly negative index keeps the array so the
#     message can name its length.
#   - casts (compiler): "class java.lang.String cannot be cast to class java.lang.Integer (java.lang.String
#     and java.lang.Integer are in module java.base of loader 'bootstrap')". A program's own classes are
#     "in unnamed module of loader com.sun.tools.javac.launcher.MemoryClassLoader @<hash>", as with
#     java Main.java; the hash is an identity hash on both sides and never matches (the JDK's changes with
#     the program and its directory). Every reached class keeps its name so the message can name it.
#   - String.charAt: "Index 5 out of bounds for length 3"; String.substring/subSequence: a
#     StringIndexOutOfBoundsException (was a bare IndexOutOfBoundsException on Wasm) with
#     "Range [2, 7) out of bounds for length 3", checked before the empty-range shortcut.
#   - Integer.parseInt, Long.parseLong: For input string: "12a" (plus " under radix 16" for another
#     radix), "Cannot parse null string", "radix 1 less than Character.MIN_RADIX".
#   - Double.parseDouble, Float.parseFloat: For input string: "abc", "multiple points", "empty String".
#   - Not changed here: Scanner.nextInt/nextLong (teavm-0005) pass parseInt/parseLong's message through,
#     so with this patch a token out of range reports the text above. That matches the JDK for a token
#     with no sign or a leading '-'; for a leading '+' the fork's message drops the '+' and the JDK's keeps
#     it (For input string: "99999999999" where the JDK says "+99999999999").
# NullPointerException's "helpful" message is left out on purpose (D11): no page shows it.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm tag 0.13.1 (b3a245b7), after teavm-0001 to teavm-0008

